Z||000000||Pretender||04-19-99||07:56 PM||||i'm charging my battery and i'm not sure if it's an ok thing to do...since we have the side mount terms. i needed like two bolts so i could clamp on them...i used two 4 inch deck screws which aren't big enough(laying in the holes but making contact)...if this is very dangerous and stupid please reply....this is the first time it went dead and it's my fault...i didn't tighten the alternator tight enough when i installed the power pully.....:o(<br>
Z||000001||Patrick||04-19-99||09:29 PM||||<br>I wouldn't have come right out and said it was a "<b>stupid</b>" thing to do, but since you said it first, I'll have to agree. <p>When a battery is being charged, explosive gases are being formed. Why the hell would you use screws that are simply "laying in the holes" when you're charging the battery? Are you hoping to collect the insurance money when one of the screws slip and a spark triggers an explosion? I don't think you really want a face full of battery acid. You might find it difficult to drive your Fiero if you've been blinded.<p>I don't know off hand what the bolt size is of the bolts that connect the battery cables to the battery, but there is nothing special or exotic about these bolts. Go to a hardware store and buy a couple. Just put them in finger tight. If you crank them in you'll crack the battery case.<p>In the meantime,<p><b>TURN OFF THE FRIGGEN BATTERY CHARGER AND DISCONNECT IT FROM THE BATTERY !!!</b><p>On second thought, I <b>would</b> have come right out and said what a <b>stupid</b> thing that was for you to do.<p><br>   
