Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||04-20-99||01:43 PM||||Well EMF, we all do the stupidest thing from time to time. I'm no exception, I keep my fire extinguisher in the engine compartment!!! (I still haven't found the time to build it in the front compartment instead)<p>I can understand Pretender though. It happens to me everytime I work on my car. Sometimes I encounter something for which I need a very simple part, like a bolt or a tool which I can get for a few bucks at the store down the road. But I'm impatient and want to get it done immediately and try to do it with the parts/tools at hand. I usually end up breaking more things than I fix...<p><i>"Dammit Jim, I'm a programmer - not a car mechanic"</i>  ;)
